  "story": {
    "sceneNotes": {
      "v": [
        "B50 Disco (ra_disco_01): Straßenparty, bpm 100, HIT 1 alle Chicken Dance",
        "B50 Gunfight r2: Spielzeugsoldat aus B11 r5c (Trage-Gewehr ab), Karabiner einhändig auf der Unterarmachse (Option A, q132)",
        "B50 Gunfight: Spielzeugsoldat aus B11 r5c mit dem Pack-Gewehr im KayKit-Kit-Slot handslot.r. r3d (Georg 20.10., V-581/V-582): Zielen/Schießen/Nachladen mit beiden Händen am Gewehr, ganze Figur vom Host um die Laufabweichung gedreht; Laufen/seitlich/kleiner Treffer/Ruhe mit natürlicher Haltung je Clip; Ausweichen und großer Treffer mit Oberkörper aus Laufen-mit-Gewehr; Sterbe-Clips lassen das Gewehr fallen (r3b-Fallbahn)",
        "V-464 (Georg 18.10.): Trupp aus sechs Aufzieh-Zinnsoldaten, Nummer groß am Tschako; Dalton-Gag: Nr. 1 ist der Anführer und der Kleinste, Nr. 6 der Größte. Die r2-Schirmmütze bleibt als eigene Rolle „Verkehrspolizist“ (B11 r2)."
      ],
      "src": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/BUEHNE_R2/scenelets/disco_street_01/disco_soldier.figure.json#story; KFB_HUB/50_BLENDER/K12/data/disco_soldier.k12.figure.json#story; KFB_HUB/50_BLENDER/B50/_work/toysoldier_duel_r3b.figure.vor_r3c.json#story; KFB_HUB/50_BLENDER/N15/data/toysoldier_duel_r3d.n15.figure.json#story; KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/BUEHNE_R2/scenelets/toy_soldier_parade_01/toy_soldier_squad.figure.r4.json#story",
      "status": "SOURCE"
    },
    "inWorldRole": {
      "v": "Wach-Resident · Parade / Spielzeug",
      "src": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/RESIDENT_ATLAS_S17_1to1/data/cast.js#RESIDENTS.toy-soldier.townRole",
      "status": "SOURCE"
    },
    "loreStatements": {
      "v": [
        {
          "text": "The KFB universe may be experienced as a **cosmic casting**. A figure may imagine, believe, recall or in individual authored lore actually have chosen *this* role for their immortal soul: the recurring Orc, the restless Graveyard skeleton, the toy soldier, the unsuccessful schemer, the obsessive banker, the hopeful farmer. The cosmic job matters to them precisely because their flaws, hardships, compulsions, embarrassment and minor triumphs constitute *their* part of the ensemble.",
          "file": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md",
          "line": 88,
          "heading": "A. Ontological frame: chosen, assigned, celebrated"
        },
        {
          "text": "**In character / on duty:** the Orc hurls himself into another hopeless battle; the undead skeleton haunts its cemetery; a toy soldier embodies the petty, procedural banality of authority; the banker sincerely worships his ledgers. They act in-world and accept real scene stakes and consequences. Combat, fear, solidarity, injury, coercion and responsibility are not fake merely because the performance has Kayfabe form.",
          "file": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md",
          "line": 95,
          "heading": "B. Two equally true social registers"
        },
        {
          "text": "Their delight derives from **being-in-the-world, doing what they do, embracing or humorously reflecting their own sometimes deeply dysfunctional character mask**. An Orc, Evil Mage, Trickster, Graveyard revenant, Toy Soldier, resident builder or socially awkward authority can find joy and a sense of vocation in inhabiting that part with full Kayfabe conviction. They welcome a returning player as a fellow participant in a game they are already energetically playing. The character can challenge, o",
          "file": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md",
          "line": 225,
          "heading": "A. Correct ontological relation — existence and joy before the audience"
        }
      ],
      "src": "KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md:88; KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md:95; KFB_HUB/30_DECISIONS/replies/WS0_GLOBAL_INTENT_ROLE_CONSCIOUS_RESIDENTS_R1_2026-10-15.md:225",
      "status": "PREFILL"
    }
  },
